  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463166",
      "title": "Events & Methods",
      "lectureOrder": 24,
      "videoOrder": 20,
      "sourceHash": "0a005ef0c6dde50109e0ae85fcc2a7a237041eea36e1f3b57b37e3b1d1843367",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.91,
          "en": "Now we learned how to listen to events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.91,
          "end": 6.84,
          "en": "Now here's one important thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.84,
          "end": 11.17,
          "en": "Currently, I'm updating the counter here in my HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.17,
          "end": 15.1,
          "en": "In the Vue control parts, but in the HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.1,
          "end": 19.38,
          "en": "and it's generally is considered a bad",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.38,
          "end": 23.13,
          "en": "or not optimal practice to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.13,
          "end": 28.07,
          "en": "You don't wanna put too much logic into your HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.07,
          "end": 30.27,
          "en": "Instead, the HTML code should really",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.27,
          "end": 32.483,
          "en": "just be about outputting stuff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.72,
          "end": 36.58,
          "en": "Logic like this, even though it's not too complex,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.58,
          "end": 39.77,
          "en": "should typically go into your JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.77,
          "end": 44.363,
          "en": "Now how could we get this logic into our JavaScript code?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.49,
          "end": 48.37,
          "en": "Well, we wanna do something on every click.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.37,
          "end": 49.89,
          "en": "What do you typically use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.89,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "if you wanna do something at a certain point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 56.43,
          "en": "potentially in a repeated way?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.43,
          "end": 58.69,
          "en": "Well, you need a function that can be called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.69,
          "end": 59.63,
          "en": "You need a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.63,
          "end": 61.92,
          "en": "which you can call when the Add button is clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.92,
          "end": 63.61,
          "en": "and you need a function which you can call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.61,
          "end": 65.31,
          "en": "when the Reduce button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.42,
          "end": 71.42,
          "en": "Now of course, we could specify a function here, add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 75.01,
          "en": "and there, try to set counter equal to counter plus one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.01,
          "end": 76.39,
          "en": "But for multiple reasons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.39,
          "end": 77.69,
          "en": "this wouldn't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.69,
          "end": 81.32,
          "en": "for one counter is not a globally available variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.32,
          "end": 83.22,
          "en": "it is a data property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.22,
          "end": 85.4,
          "en": "hence it's not available here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.4,
          "end": 87.56,
          "en": "In addition, even if it would be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.56,
          "end": 88.95,
          "en": "for whatever reason,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.95,
          "end": 93.35,
          "en": "add now is a globally created function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.35,
          "end": 96.68,
          "en": "But in your Vue controlled HTML code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.68,
          "end": 98.78,
          "en": "you can't use such a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.78,
          "end": 103.33,
          "en": "You can only use in this Vue controlled HTML part,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.33,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "what is defined in your Vue app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 108.55,
          "en": "And that's why we use methods for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.55,
          "end": 111.28,
          "en": "and we did already learn about methods before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.28,
          "end": 115,
          "en": "Now, we don't just use methods to manually call them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115,
          "end": 118.84,
          "en": "as we did before, we can also use methods to connect them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.84,
          "end": 122.14,
          "en": "to event listeners and let Vue call them for us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.14,
          "end": 124.26,
          "en": "when a certain event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.26,
          "end": 127.18,
          "en": "For example, here, we can add a add method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.18,
          "end": 130.06,
          "en": "though this name here is totally up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.06,
          "end": 133.18,
          "en": "you could also name it add counter or increment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.18,
          "end": 135.7,
          "en": "or whatever you want, but I'll name it add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.7,
          "end": 140.03,
          "en": "And in here, you can now update this counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.03,
          "end": 144.1,
          "en": "just important as you learned with this counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.1,
          "end": 145.53,
          "en": "In your JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.53,
          "end": 149.51,
          "en": "you refer to your data properties with this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.51,
          "end": 151.51,
          "en": "This counter plus plus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.51,
          "end": 154.24,
          "en": "or the longer form this counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.24,
          "end": 157.76,
          "en": "equals this counter plus one, it's the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.76,
          "end": 161.39,
          "en": "And with that, we have a method which we can call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.39,
          "end": 163.44,
          "en": "to update our counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.44,
          "end": 165.43,
          "en": "Now this method doesn't return anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.43,
          "end": 167.12,
          "en": "because it doesn't have to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.12,
          "end": 170.04,
          "en": "We'll not use the method like we did before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.04,
          "end": 172.96,
          "en": "to dynamically output something here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.96,
          "end": 177.32999999999998,
          "en": "Instead, we're using it to run it when a click occurs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 177.32999999999998,
          "end": 179.57,
          "en": "and therefore, this does need to return anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.57,
          "end": 183.37,
          "en": "because the click listener doesn't want a return value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.37,
          "end": 187.35,
          "en": "So now here, we can call add like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.35,
          "end": 190.45,
          "en": "and if I now saved it and reload, I can click add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.45,
          "end": 194.01,
          "en": "and it still works because we're executing the same code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.01,
          "end": 196.04,
          "en": "just in a different way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.04,
          "end": 198.99,
          "en": "And this is actually the batter way of doing it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.99,
          "end": 201.2,
          "en": "putting your logic into JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.2,
          "end": 203.64,
          "en": "and just pointing at that logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.64,
          "end": 206.55,
          "en": "That is generally considered better,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.55,
          "end": 209.72,
          "en": "even though technically, it here works in the same way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.72,
          "end": 213.17000000000002,
          "en": "But consider cases where you have more complex logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.17000000000002,
          "end": 216.11,
          "en": "and it quickly makes sense that you should put that logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 216.11,
          "end": 219.35,
          "en": "into JavaScript and not into HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 219.35,
          "end": 222.22,
          "en": "So it's not bad to get started with that as a habit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 222.22,
          "end": 223.413,
          "en": "right from the start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 225.1,
          "end": 228.23,
          "en": "Now besides calling add like this, by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.23,
          "end": 230.66,
          "en": "you can also just point at it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.66,
          "end": 233.927,
          "en": "so that you tell Vue, \"Hey, that's the name of the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 233.927,
          "end": 236.337,
          "en": "\"or of the method to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 236.337,
          "end": 238.94,
          "en": "\"You should execute when a click occurs.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.94,
          "end": 243.53,
          "en": "Vue accepts both, you explicitly calling it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 243.53,
          "end": 245.46,
          "en": "or you pointing at it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.46,
          "end": 247.33,
          "en": "Vue detects what you're doing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 247.33,
          "end": 249.923,
          "en": "and it will do the right thing in both cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 250.82,
          "end": 253.22,
          "en": "Now typically, you just wanna point at it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 253.22,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "since that is closer to vanilla JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 256.2,
          "end": 259.03,
          "en": "and how you would set up an event listener there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 259.03,
          "end": 263.11,
          "en": "but it is worth noting that both syntaxes are allowed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 263.11,
          "end": 264.86,
          "en": "as you can see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 264.86,
          "end": 268.513,
          "en": "Well, and now let's do the same for reducing our counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 269.37,
          "end": 270.76,
          "en": "Of course, try this on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 270.76,
          "end": 272.65,
          "en": "Here's a quick pause for you to do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 272.65,
          "end": 274.55,
          "en": "and there after, we'll do it together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 277.38,
          "end": 278.90999999999997,
          "en": "Were you successful?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 278.90999999999997,
          "end": 281.87,
          "en": "Well, again, it's pretty much the same code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 281.87,
          "end": 285.53,
          "en": "We can add a reduce method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 285.53,
          "end": 287.61,
          "en": "again, this name is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 287.61,
          "end": 289.47,
          "en": "and in there, we just set this counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 289.47,
          "end": 293.94,
          "en": "equal to this counter minus one, or we use the shorter form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 293.94,
          "end": 296.08299999999997,
          "en": "which looks like this, which is also okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 298.5,
          "end": 301.73,
          "en": "And now in here on this second button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 301.73,
          "end": 306.02,
          "en": "we can call reduce like this, or as I just mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 306.02,
          "end": 308.57,
          "en": "just point at it, both is accepted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 308.57,
          "end": 311.02,
          "en": "And now we've got our working buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 311.02,
          "end": 312.8,
          "en": "with one important change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 312.8,
          "end": 316.82,
          "en": "now the logic is outsourced into JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 316.82,
          "end": 319.16,
          "en": "which is where your logic should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 319.16,
          "end": 322.46,
          "en": "and the HTML code is cleaner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 322.46,
          "end": 323.75,
          "en": "and this is better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 323.75,
          "end": 325.4,
          "en": "This is considered to be better,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 325.4,
          "end": 328.86,
          "en": "so it is a good idea to get started with this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 328.86,
          "end": 330.453,
          "en": "and with this pattern.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 332.32,
          "end": 335.38,
          "en": "Now that is how we can use methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 335.38,
          "end": 340.34000000000003,
          "en": "We cannot just use them in curly braces or with the bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 340.34000000000003,
          "end": 344.2,
          "en": "to dynamically derive a value we wanna output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 344.2,
          "end": 347.36,
          "en": "but we can also use them with event listeners",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 347.36,
          "end": 349.74,
          "en": "to define codes that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 349.74,
          "end": 352.01,
          "en": "when the event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 352.01,
          "end": 355.53,
          "en": "And in reality, you will more often use methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 355.53,
          "end": 357.15999999999997,
          "en": "to connect them to events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 357.15999999999997,
          "end": 358.42,
          "en": "than you will use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 358.42,
          "end": 361.03,
          "en": "to output something dynamically derived.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 361.03,
          "end": 364.36,
          "en": "I just showed this before to show you that it's possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 364.36,
          "end": 366.28,
          "en": "and to introduce methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 366.28,
          "end": 368.66,
          "en": "but typically, you'll use them like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 368.66,
          "end": 370.543,
          "en": "in combination with event listeners.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
